---
import Footer from "../components/footer.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/nav.astro";

const github = "https://github.com/adriangohjw/storybranch";

const workflow = `${github}/blob/main/examples/github-actions/visual-regression.yml`;
const commentScript = `${github}/blob/main/scripts/ci/storybranch-pr-comment.mjs`;
const ciDoc = `${github}/blob/main/docs/ci.md`;
---

<Layout
  title="CI — storybranch"
  description="Run storybranch in GitHub Actions: build Storybook, capture with --exit-once, upload artifacts, and review failures locally."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-5 py-12 sm:px-8 sm:py-16">
    <p class="text-accent text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide uppercase">
      Continuous integration
    </p>
    <h1
      class="font-syne text-ink mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl"
    >
      GitHub Actions
    </h1>
    <p class="text-ink-muted mt-4 text-lg">
      storybranch in CI is a test: build Storybook, capture snapshots, exit
      <strong class="text-ink font-semibold">1</strong> when a shot needs
      attention. Approval stays on a machine where someone can run
      <code class="text-ink">storybranch review</code>. There is no hosted
      review URL.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-syne text-ink mt-12 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">
      Copy-paste recipe
    </h2>
    <p class="text-ink-muted mt-4">
      Start from the example workflow and PR comment script in the repo (Node.js
      22.18+):
    </p>
    <ul class="text-ink-muted mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
      <li>
        <a
          class="text-ink decoration-ink/20 hover:decoration-ink/50 underline underline-offset-2"
          href={workflow}
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank"
          >visual-regression.yml</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          class="text-ink decoration-ink/20 hover:decoration-ink/50 underline underline-offset-2"
          href={commentScript}
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank"
          >storybranch-pr-comment.mjs</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          class="text-ink decoration-ink/20 hover:decoration-ink/50 underline underline-offset-2"
          href={ciDoc}
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank"
          >docs/ci.md</a
        > — monorepos, extra browsers, and how this repo’s own CI job works
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-syne text-ink mt-12 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">
      What the job does
    </h2>
    <ol class="text-ink-muted mt-4 list-decimal space-y-3 pl-5">
      <li>
        Check out with <code class="text-ink">fetch-depth: 0</code> so
        <code class="text-ink">--only-changed</code> can find the merge base.
      </li>
      <li>
        Install dependencies and
        <code class="text-ink"
          >npx playwright install --with-deps chromium</code
        >
        (GitHub-hosted runners need system libraries).
      </li>
      <li>
        <code class="text-ink">npx storybook build</code>, then
        <code class="text-ink"
          >npx storybranch test --build --exit-once</code
        >. Pull requests add <code class="text-ink">--only-changed</code>;
        pushes to <code class="text-ink">main</code> capture every story.
      </li>
      <li>
        On failure, upload
        <code class="text-ink">report.json</code>,
        <code class="text-ink">actual/</code>, and
        <code class="text-ink">diff/</code> as one artifact. Baselines stay in
        git.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <pre
      class="border-ink/10 bg-paper-2 mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed"
    ><code>npx storybook build
npx storybranch test --build --only-changed --exit-once</code></pre>

    <h2 class="font-syne text-ink mt-12 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">
      Flags that matter in CI
    </h2>
    <ul class="text-ink-muted mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
      <li>
        <code class="text-ink">--exit-once</code> — print results and skip the
        review server. Without it, a failed run can hang until the job times
        out.
      </li>
      <li>
        Do not pass <code class="text-ink">--review</code> or
        <code class="text-ink">--open</code> in CI.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code class="text-ink">--only-changed</code> uses
        <code class="text-ink">GITHUB_BASE_REF</code> on pull requests, otherwise
        <code class="text-ink">origin/main</code>. Lockfile or workflow edits
        still capture every story.
      </li>
      <li>
        CI does not accept snapshots. Update
        <code class="text-ink">.storybranch/baseline/</code> locally (
        <code class="text-ink">storybranch approve</code> or the review UI) and
        commit.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-syne text-ink mt-12 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">
      After a failed run
    </h2>
    <p class="text-ink-muted mt-4">
      Download the workflow artifact, unpack it into the Storybook package, and
      run <code class="text-ink">storybranch review</code>. The example PR
      comment lists shots that need attention and links to the workflow run.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-syne text-ink mt-12 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">
      Monorepos
    </h2>
    <p class="text-ink-muted mt-4">
      Each Storybook app keeps its own
      <code class="text-ink">.storybranch/</code>. Build and test from that
      package with <code class="text-ink">--cwd</code> (or
      <code class="text-ink">STORYBRANCH_ROOT</code>):
    </p>
    <pre
      class="border-ink/10 bg-paper-2 mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed"
    ><code>npx storybook build --config-dir apps/web/.storybook \
  --output-dir apps/web/storybook-static
npx storybranch test --build --cwd apps/web --exit-once</code></pre>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
